{
  "_doc": [
    "cross-lang-equivalents.json — manually-curated equivalences across the four sources.",
    "",
    "Format: { entries: { '<key>': { ...fields }, ... } }",
    "",
    "Each entry MAY have (use whichever fields fit):",
    "  hebrew_lemma:   Hebrew lemma (modern script) — e.g. 'יהושע'",
    "  hebrew_paleo:   Paleo-Hebrew rendering — e.g. '𐤉𐤄𐤅𐤔𐤏'",
    "  greek_lemma:    Greek lemma (LXX/GNT, accents preserved) — e.g. 'Ἰησοῦς'",
    "  greek_surface:  Greek surface form (also accepted)",
    "  geez_lemma:     Ge'ez lemma (Ethiopic script) — e.g. 'ኢየሱስ'",
    "  canonical_eng:  Your preferred English rendering — e.g. 'Yahawashai'",
    "  aliases:        Array of alternate spellings/forms to also resolve to this entry",
    "  notes:          Free-form linguistic / etymological notes",
    "  refs:           Array of representative verse refs — e.g. ['LXX|6|1|1', 'GNT|40|1|1']",
    "",
    "Keys can be any identifier (we recommend lowercase canonical English or a romanized lemma).",
    "The server's /api/cross-lang-equivalents endpoint accepts ?word=<anything> and resolves by",
    "checking the entry key first, then scanning all field values + aliases.",
    "",
    "When the UI shows a token in any source, it queries this map. If found, it offers a",
    "one-click link to the equivalent token in other sources.",
    ""
  ],
